<title>UK: Daiwa Europe, London wins Reuter Feb FX poll.</title>
<headline>Daiwa Europe, London wins Reuter Feb FX poll.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daiwa Europe in London won the Reuter February foreign exchange poll, with an average divergence from the actual rate of 1.2470 percent A total of 30 banks and financial institutions from across the globe were polled.</p>
<p>Yamaichi in London came second with 1.2675 percent followed by Bank of Montreal in Toronto, with 1.3653 percent divergence rates.</p>
<p>Overall, the percentage divergence between actual and forecast rates varied between 1.2470 and 3.4866 percent.</p>
<p>The rankings were based on the accuracy of the forecasts against the European closing rates on February 28 of dollar/mark at 1.6881, dollar/yen at 120.53 and sterling/dollar at 1.6280.</p>
